---
source: crates/dreamd-cli/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: "subcommand_help(\"mcp\")"
---
Start the MCP server, bridged to the running daemon or, on Unix, in-process when none is running

Usage: mcp [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --manual-only
          Hard-lock dream cycle to manual-only mode (overrides config.toml)

      --project-root <PATH>
          Use the `.agent/` store in this folder instead of discovering one from the working directory. Needed when the IDE launches the MCP server from a non-project CWD (e.g. Cursor's global ~/.cursor/mcp.json). The folder must hold `.agent/` itself. A relative path is resolved against the working directory, and a leading `~` is not expanded. If the folder holds no store, or its `.agent/` is the daemon home, `dreamd mcp` exits 2

      --bind <ADDR>
          Serve MCP over Streamable HTTP at http://ADDR/mcp instead of stdio: an IP or IP:port, e.g. `127.0.0.1:8080` or `[::1]:0`. Port defaults to 0 (OS-chosen). Hostnames are not resolved. No auth: any local process can reach a loopback bind. Needs a build with the `mcp-http` cargo feature (prebuilt release binaries are stdio-only)

      --insecure
          Allow a non-loopback --bind. Logs a warning on every start and accepts any Host header. Requires --bind

  -h, --help
          Print help
